        "id": 3910751306,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "**[P2] Save the completed quest together with the irreversible conversion**\n\nLocation: `src/quest/quest.c:692-693` (`convert_to_descend_form`). This save happens before `complete_quest()` calls `add_completed_quest()`, `clear_quest()`, and `set_quest()` for the next stage (lines 919-935); neither the remainder of that function nor the `eQUEST_COMPLETE` handler saves afterward. A crash/restart before the next unrelated character save therefore keeps the new race, zero XP, and rewards, but restores the conversion quest as unfinished. The new preflight then prevents completing it again, and any following stage is lost.\n\n**Repro:** Run `TestDescendFormConversionSucceedsAndSurvivesReload` and inspect `loaded` before `free_char(loaded)` at test line 2195. At this MR head I get `loaded->player.race == 56`, `saved.current_quest == {701, 0, 0}`, and `saved.num_completed_quests == 0`, while the source character has completed quest 701. The existing test checks the source's quest completion, but not the reloaded character's.\n\n**Fix:** Commit the final character save after the quest history, active slot, and next stage have all been updated, before any follower callback can extract the owner. Extend the reload test to assert completed history and the active/next quest slot as well as race/XP.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
