      {
        "id": 3910751618,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "**[P2] Enforce the one-way transformation rule on the existing conversion paths too**\n\nLocation: `src/quest/quest.c:753-754`. The already-transformed check only runs when the *destination* is one of the five new forms. A level-30 Wight/Revenant/etc. can still complete a Lich or Vampire race reward: `find_descend_form_conversion()` returns NULL, so the guard is skipped and the existing switch overwrites the form, rebuilds the character, and clears its XP. The legacy Lich quest in `src/quest/hlquest.c` and the Lich rite in `src/spec/spec_rol_conversion.c` likewise have no check for a descend-form source. This contradicts the new preflight's stated rule that transformed races cannot become another form and the documented irreversible acquisition.\n\n**Repro:** In `TestDescendFormConversionSucceedsAndSurvivesReload`, change only the second reward from `RACE_REVENANT` to `RACE_LICH` (or set `quest.quest.race_reward = 45` at the breakpoint on test line 2187). The Wight is converted to a Lich and the final assertion fails: `expected <56> but was <45>`. I reproduced this on the MR head.\n\n**Fix:** Validate the source's transformation status before dispatching *any* race conversion, and apply the same restriction to the other Lich entry points. Add tests for new-form-to-Lich and new-form-to-Vampire attempts, asserting that race, XP, rewards, and quest state remain unchanged.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
        },
