      {
        "id": 3910804637,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Fixed in 6446f4af8, on all three entry points.\n\n- `complete_quest()`: the transformation-only check moved out of `descend_form_preflight()` into the general race-reward preflight, so it runs before any conversion is dispatched (Lich, Vampire, or form). `descend_form_preflight()` keeps only the class requirement.\n- `src/quest/hlquest.c` legacy Lich quest: refuses a transformation-only real race and returns the offerings.\n- `src/spec/spec_rol_conversion.c` Lich rite: new `ROL_LICH_RITE_ALREADY_TRANSFORMED`, checked right after the invalid-actor check, so nothing is consumed.\n\nTests:\n- `TestDescendFormConversionPreflightChangesNothing` adds Wight to Lich, Wight to Vampire, Lich to Vampire, and Vampire to Lich, each asserting race, class, level, XP, alignment, gold, and quest state are unchanged.\n- The reload test now retries the converted Wight against Revenant, Lich, and Vampire rewards at level 30 with warrior levels, asserting race, XP, gold, the quest slot, and history do not change. Your Lich repro fails on the previous head.\n- New `TestLegacyLichQuestRefusesATransformedCharacter` drives `quest_give()` for Wight, Phantom, Vampire, and Lich.\n- `Test_spec_rol_lich_rite_validates_irreversible_conversion_preflight` checks the new status, and that a Wight with every other requirement met is refused without consuming the offerings or the keeper.\n\nThe race guide, race reference, spec-proc guide, and quest file format now state the one-way rule for all conversions.",
