        "id": 3910805092,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Both review findings are fixed in 6446f4af8 and their threads are resolved:\n\n- Race conversions now save together with the quest history and next stage.\n- Transformation is one-way on every conversion path: race rewards, the legacy Lich quest, and the Lich rite.\n\nVerification on the head (6446f4af8):\n- The branch sits directly on master (4adcab7a0), so no rebase was needed.\n- `make test`: 1836 CuTest cases pass.\n- The full local CI matrix passes, 33 of 33 jobs, including the sanitizers, memory check, coverage, clang-tidy, format, hygiene, world validation, and database migration.\n\nThis is ready to merge. I recommend the project's regular merge commit rather than a squash. The nine commits are each self-contained: shared mechanics, creation races, descend forms, help, docs, retiring the plan, the link-drop crash fix, and the review fixes. Keeping them separate keeps `git blame` pointing at the change that explains each line.",
